60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option A is what we did before, and it was a mess because we guessed the number. I think Option B gives us more stability.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option C might be too much of a barrier. If people have to decide to pay every time they come, they might just stay home.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"Option C is the only one that's fair. If you don't come, you don't pay. The people who are here every week shouldn't subsidize the ghosts.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option C is a disaster for the treasurer. Chasing small payments for every single event is exactly what we need to avoid.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Option C sounds scary for new people! They'd have to worry about money every time they visit. Option A is simple, but maybe too much at once.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, I totally agree. Option C is a nightmare. Option B lets us set a ""base"" cost for the hall hire and then extra for those who want more.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I fear Option C will only increase the hesitancy I mentioned. Option A is the most welcoming, as the cost is forgotten once paid.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, ""forgetting"" the cost is why people stop coming! They don't value it. Option C makes them value the activity.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"Option A is the only sustainable choice for the administration. One payment, one record. It prevents the treasurer from spending their evenings on a spreadsheet.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"I like Option B! It's like a ""taster"" level for new people and a ""full"" level for the regulars. It's a good middle ground!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Kenji, exactly! Option B allows us to calculate the minimum we need to survive and then add a bit more for the active members.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I can see the merit in Option B. It provides a low-pressure entry point while still maintaining a sense of membership.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Takumi,,Option B is just a fancy version of Option A. It still doesn't solve the problem of the same dozen people doing all the work.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is acceptable, provided the tiers are set at the start of the year. As long as we aren't chasing payments weekly, it works.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"Let's go with B! It's friendly, it's flexible, and it doesn't make the treasurer cry!","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm feeling really good about Option B. It solves the ""guesswork"" problem by letting us set a base fee for the essentials.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. It removes the immediate friction of a high entry fee while avoiding the constant decision-making of Option C.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"I still think it's unfair, but if the alternative is a treasurer who quits in a month, I guess B is the only realistic choice.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"I am satisfied with Option B, provided the payment is collected upfront for the year.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,Yay! I think we all agree that we want the club to stay happy and easy to join.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
